.TH AD-DEBUG-BUNDLE 1 "2026-08-21" "diffvim 2.0" "diffvim Manual"
.SH NAME
ad_debug_bundle \- Generate a debug bundle for reporting ad issues
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_debug_bundle
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.br
.B ad_debug_bundle
.I oldfile
.I newfile
.RI [ description ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ad_debug_bundle
runs the full diffvim pipeline (compute \[->] postprocess \[->] pace \[->]
decorate \[->] animator) on the given old/new file pair, then packages
every intermediate stage output, the binary MD5s, the active settings,
system info, and the user-supplied problem description into a single
tar.gz archive.
.PP
The resulting bundle contains everything a maintainer needs to reproduce
and debug an issue \(em no need to manually collect logs or run multiple
commands.
.PP
The bundle is written to
.I /tmp/diffvim_debug_<timestamp>.tar.gz
and the path is printed to stdout.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Show the help message and exit 0.
.TP
.I oldfile
Path to the original/source file (required).
.TP
.I newfile
Path to the target file (required).
.TP
.I description
Optional free-text description of the problem (default: "No description provided.").
.SH BUNDLE CONTENTS
The tar.gz archive contains the following files:
.TP
.I old.txt
Copy of the input old file.
.TP
.I new.txt
Copy of the input new file.
.TP
.I raw_ops.txt
Stage 1 \(em compute output (raw diff ops).
.TP
.I post_ops.txt
Stage 2 \(em postprocess output.
.TP
.I timed_ops.txt
Stage 3 \(em pace output (timed ops).
.TP
.I decorated_ops.txt
Stage 4 \(em decorate output (if available).
.TP
.I animator_output.txt
Final animator output buffer.
.TP
.I output_diff.txt
Diff between expected (newfile) and actual.
.TP
.I binary_md5s.txt
MD5 checksums of all pipeline binaries.
.TP
.I settings.conf
Default diffvim launcher settings.
.TP
.I system_info.txt
OS, vim, perl, gcc, git commit/branch.
.TP
.I description.txt
User-supplied problem description.
.TP
.I op_counts.txt
Op counts per stage + \[rs]n delete counts.
.TP
.I *_stderr.txt
stderr captured from each pipeline stage.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Generate a bundle with the default description:
.B ad_debug_bundle old.py new.py
.TP
Generate a bundle with a specific problem description:
.B ad_debug_bundle old.py new.py "Cursor jumps to wrong line after \[rs]n delete"
.TP
Reproduce the scattered-LCS bug for the maintainer:
.br
.B ad_debug_bundle tests/tests/examples/02_large_python/old.py \[rs]
.br
.B                         tests/tests/examples/02_large_python/new.py \[rs]
.br
.B                         "Line 7 shows 'O operation.' instead of 'O'"
.SH OUTPUT
.I /tmp/diffvim_debug_<YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS>.tar.gz
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
0
Bundle created successfully.
.TP
1
Invalid arguments or pipeline failure.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR diffvim (1),
.BR ad_compute (1),
.BR ad (1),
.BR snapshot_per_op (1)
